Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 0.1.  The pipeline this notebook implements \
end-to-end: text becomes BPE tokens; tokens become integer IDs; two embedding \
layers turn IDs into vectors; a stack of transformer blocks processes the \
vectors; the head projects back to a probability distribution over the \
vocabulary.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"963eebb1-422f-4397-bedf-\
4bc6d7f3f71d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every modern language model \[LongDash] GPT-2, Llama, Mistral, the ",
 "model you talk to in the wild \[LongDash] is fundamentally the same ",
 "function: a sequence of ",
 Cell[BoxData["n"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"e3bdfbdc-fe9d-4676-9555-fa4ec098318d"],
 " integer token IDs goes in, a sequence of probability ",
 "distributions over a vocabulary of size ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"|", "V", "|"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"9c9094b1-27bf-47dd-996b-31058b840d4b"],
 " comes out.  What changes between systems is the size of the ",
 "matrices and the training regime, not the shape of the function."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"08795209-3956-4dba-b905-7403a8355511"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The notebook proceeds linearly through the pipeline above.  Each ",
 "section introduces one piece, derives whatever needs deriving, ",
 "implements it as a Wolfram Language ",
 StyleBox["NetGraph",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", and uses it.  By ",
 "the end of Chapter ",
 StyleBox["4",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " you have a model architecture; by Chapter ",
 StyleBox["5",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " you have a trained model that produces text; by Chapter ",
 StyleBox["7",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " you have a model that follows instructions and can be chatted ",
 "with from inside the notebook."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f1356fc5-56d8-4b87-9150-0766a44eb78a"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"06cc217d-ef77-4bff-86f7-9753350cda6f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The notebook expects to be opened from its repository directory; ",
 StyleBox["NotebookDirectory[]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " is used to anchor every file path.  No global PATH or environment ",
 "variable is required."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"69602bec-e248-4491-90ed-c74d62c03bf4"],

Cell["SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"838551c2-279e-48d7-9c49-ff5fa8049b95"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All of the auxiliary functions used across the notebook live in a ",
 "single companion file, ",
 StyleBox["LLMAtoZ.wl",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", at the repo root.  Each chapter's helpers live in their own ",
 "context (",
 StyleBox["LLMAtoZ`Tokeniser`",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["LLMAtoZ`Attention`",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", \[Ellipsis], ",
 StyleBox["LLMAtoZ`Discussion`",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ") so you can tell which chapter a symbol comes from.  ",
 "If you'd rather see each chapter's source on its own, the file is ",
 "auto-generated from the per-part packages in ",
 StyleBox["part-NN/src/",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "; run ",
 StyleBox["wolframscript -file build_LLMAtoZ_wl.wls",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " to regenerate."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"95ef6079-d9c8-406a-9914-5c02fd145852"],

Cell["Get[\"LLMAtoZ.wl\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4ec33e29-97dd-4ea8-89d9-5a25c7ca70f2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Load the corpus.  Tiny Shakespeare is a 1.1-megabyte concatenation ",
 "of public-domain Shakespeare play text, originally assembled by ",
 "Andrej Karpathy for ",
 StyleBox["char-rnn",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (2015) and used as a benchmark across the literature ever since.  ",
 "It is small enough to train on, large enough that BPE produces a ",
 "non-trivial vocabulary, and out of copyright."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4568441d-6cca-41a2-b4dd-cc74d837443b"],

Cell["\<\
text = Import[\"part-01-tokeniser-and-embeddings/data/tinyshakespeare.txt\", \
\"Text\"];
{StringLength[text], \"characters\"}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"00833cd8-7857-45a9-b8bb-feca2908a731"],

Cell["\<\
About 1.1 million characters.  About 250,000 whitespace-separated words.  65 \
distinct characters (upper- and lower-case letters, digits, punctuation, \
whitespace, newline).  Three numbers that will reappear throughout the \
notebook.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"27d31d28-1963-45e3-925b-12545a1a6c69"],

Cell["A map of the whole notebook", "Subsection", CellTags -> "PART9-FLOWCHART"],

Cell["The notebook follows three paths to a working model. Path A trains the original GPT architecture on Tiny Shakespeare; Path B reuses OpenAI's pretrained GPT-2 weights for fine-tuning, RL, and the discussion model; Path C (Chapter 11, new) pretrains a model from scratch on cloud GPUs. The chart shows each model and the chapter where it is built.", "Text", CellTags -> "PART9-FLOWCHART"],

