Box[{{8.075, -1.7}, {8.924999999999999, -1.7}}]}, {RGBColor[0.2, 0.4, 0.65], Arrowheads[0.014], Thickness[0.0016], ArrowBox[{{1.275, -6.5}, {2.125, -6.5}}]}, {RGBColor[0.16, 0.52, 0.34], Arrowheads[0.014], Thickness[0.0016], ArrowBox[{{4.675, -6.5}, {5.525, -6.5}}]}, {RGBColor[0.45, 0.2, 0.55], Arrowheads[0.014], Thickness[0.0016], ArrowBox[{{8.075, -6.5}, {8.924999999999999, -6.5}}]}, {RGBColor[0.16, 0.52, 0.34], Arrowheads[0.014], Thickness[0.0016], ArrowBox[{{10.2, -6.96}, {10.2, -7.54}}]}, InsetBox[FormBox[StyleBox["\"PATH A  —  original GPT, trained on Tiny Shakespeare\"", 8.5, Italic, RGBColor[0.16, 0.52, 0.34], StripOnInput -> False], TraditionalForm], {-1.1749999999999998, -0.75}, NCache[ImageScaled[{0, 1/2}], ImageScaled[{0, 0.5}]]], InsetBox[FormBox[StyleBox["\"PATH B  —  reuse OpenAI's pretrained GPT-2 weights\"", 8.5, Italic, RGBColor[0.7, 0.45, 0.13], StripOnInput -> False], TraditionalForm], {5.625, -0.75}, NCache[ImageScaled[{0, 1/2}], ImageScaled[{0, 0.5}]]], InsetBox[FormBox[StyleBox["\"PATH C  —  pretrain from scratch on cloud GPUs (Part 9)\"", 8.5, Italic, RGBColor[0.2, 0.4, 0.65], StripOnInput -> False], TraditionalForm], {-1.1749999999999998, -5.55}, NCache[ImageScaled[{0, 1/2}], ImageScaled[{0, 0.5}]]]}, {ImageSize -> 850, PlotRange -> {{-1.7, 11.7}, {-9., 1.2}}, ImageSize -> 980, Background -> GrayLevel[1], AspectRatio -> Automatic}]], "Output", CellTags -> "PART9-FLOWCHART", TextAlignment -> Center],

Cell["1.  Tokenisation: turning text into integers", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"9196288d-f1d2-46ad-bd44-2e8f2463d135"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A language model does not see characters or words.  It sees ",
 "integers.  The tokeniser is the function that converts between the ",
 "two: a deterministic mapping ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"text", 
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{"\[RightArrow]", " "}]}], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleStruckCapitalN]", "n"]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"57d6f315-b1b7-4f1d-b059-19b37e455684"],
 " sending text to a length-",
 Cell[BoxData["n"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"16e43907-4c7f-4c84-8c1c-d6fd54fd858f"],
 " sequence of integer IDs in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", "1", ",", " ", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"|", "V", "|"}], "}"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"86447daa-10ab-41ba-9180-7c918c4c007a"],
 ", and back.  The choice of tokeniser is the choice of two numbers ",
 "that play against each other for the rest of the pipeline: the ",
 "vocabulary size ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"|", "V", "|"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"e1cf3c88-8f7f-4dda-a14f-418417b4e73f"],
 " and the sequence length ",
 Cell[BoxData["n"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"da368a1b-84bf-41d9-9c94-5095127ebd69"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"02c6086d-07ff-4e59-801c-ca49b5fbc84e"],

Cell["1.1  Three slicing strategies", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4574528f-90dd-4742-8551-d28f0e5e2063"],

Cell["Three obvious tokenisation schemes bracket the design space.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bb97455e-1906-4ae7-8d3e-35245b5ce413"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Character-level. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Each character is its own token.  Tiny Shakespeare gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"|", "V", "|"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"8281ab63-7c95-4965-a436-a817f633f563"],
 " = 65, ",
 Cell[BoxData["n"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"0d9344ee-055b-4e18-8346-dc06a531097a"],
 " = 1.1 million.  Tiny vocabulary, gigantic sequence; the attention ",
 "block, which is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"O", "(", 
   SuperscriptBox["n", "2"], ")"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"a1e4489e-832b-4edb-8fa5-59ee52961a2d"],
 " expensive, spends almost all its compute on positional bookkeeping."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c5069964-c34a-401d-8177-0f541f987195"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Word-level. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Each whitespace-separated word is its own token.  Tiny Shakespeare ",
 "gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"|", "V", "|"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"12505f0b-bd2e-4f52-b1c9-9b86f0094432"],
 " \[TildeEqual] 14,500, ",
 Cell[BoxData["n"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"4387c001-f88a-48ea-90a8-11c4062092a9"],
 " \[TildeEqual] 252,000.  ",
 "Large vocabulary, manageable sequence; but every rare inflection ",
 "and proper noun gets a fresh ID the model sees once or twice in ",
 "training, and anything outside the vocabulary is an unrecoverable ",
 StyleBox["<UNK>",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ad80246d-8066-4e82-a3e3-3602af868560"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Subword (BPE). ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "An interior point: learn a vocabulary by repeatedly merging the ",
 "most frequent adjacent pair of symbols.  Common short words ",
 "collapse to a single token; rare words decompose into a handful of ",
 "sub-word pieces; every input \[LongDash] including out-of-corpus ",
 "characters \[LongDash] is representable, because the base alphabet ",
 "of single characters always sits at the bottom of the merge tree.  ",
 "No ",
 StyleBox["<UNK>",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ever.  ",
 "This is the algorithm GPT-2, GPT-3, Llama, and tiktoken all use."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5fa20872-247f-47c6-9ffb-51b05b17d422"],

Cell["1.2  Byte-pair encoding, from first principles", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"484b9143-889c-4caa-80cb-c339cfd8e84b"],

Cell["\<\
BPE was originally a compression algorithm proposed by Philip Gage in 1994.  \
Its transplant to neural-network text tokenisation is by Sennrich, Haddow and \
Birch (ACL 2016).  The four-line algorithm:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fbfb7578-ac8c-4fff-ab4d-ae34e7e86cf0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["1.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Start with the alphabet of base symbols (characters).\n",
 StyleBox["2.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Across the pre-tokenised corpus, count every adjacent pair of symbols.\n",
 StyleBox["3.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Treat the most frequent pair as a new symbol from now on; record the \
merge.\n",
 StyleBox["4.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Repeat until the merge budget is spent."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"18b7d35a-697c-467e-a575-9491a725b1b7"],

