Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 2.1.  Learned positional embeddings: each \
position id (1, 2, ..., n) is looked up in a learned table; the resulting \
vector is added to the token embedding at that position.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b225cc10-db55-40c3-95b2-\
acd97857395b"],

Cell["2.1  Why a sum, not a concatenation?", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"df4a17bb-06ee-4d5d-8042-3e72e835d963"],

Cell["\<\
Two reasons.  First, with the dimensions kept aligned the transformer needs \
no extra parameters to combine them; concatenation would double the input \
dimension and require the next layer to be wider.  Second, the sum is what \
falls out naturally if you ask \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]what is the right \
basis-free way to combine two pieces of information that live in the same \
vector space\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \[LongDash] either is just a vector, and \
their sum is a vector.  The model is free to learn token- and \
position-information directions that are nearly orthogonal, which is what \
trained transformers tend to do in practice.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2b2b700f-44cc-4a64-902a-205f6c06a026"],

Cell["2.2  The embedder NetGraph", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"820eb022-0ca6-43c1-91c6-cdec9afad0c3"],

Cell["\<\
embedder = LLMAtoZ`Tokeniser`tokenPositionEmbedder[
  Length[vocab], 64, 256, RandomSeeding -> 42];
embedder\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c9109648-aaf9-47dc-8629-773087ef2613"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Three nodes: token embedding, position embedding, and an ",
 "elementwise add.  Inputs are a token-ID sequence and a position-ID ",
 "sequence; output is a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"(", "seqLen", ",", " ", 
   SubscriptBox["d", "model"], ")"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"ab51d901-e77c-4be1-a786-e1c9f04a9cb8"],
 " tensor, the standard input shape of the transformer block we ",
 "build in Chapter 4."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8e25234a-6348-4bed-a84d-e5d75fb4a7ec"],

Cell["\<\
ids = LLMAtoZ`Tokeniser`encodeWithIds[
  \"To be or not to be, that is the question.\",
  mergeRules, tokId];
LLMAtoZ`Tokeniser`embedTokens[embedder, ids] // Dimensions\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a4ca5bc7-7e00-49d5-94a6-89febc8a0867"],

Cell["\<\
Twelve tokens in, a 12\[Times]64 tensor out.  That tensor is exactly what the \
first transformer block will consume.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fd500450-507b-453e-a111-ab834e2a0817"],

Cell["2.3  Geometry before training", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cf9b6f7f-18ef-44aa-ac17-516ff38d4d16"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The token-embedding row for ",
 StyleBox["\"the\"",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " right now is just a vector of 64 Gaussian noise samples.  ",
 "Whatever similarity structure the trained model will eventually ",
 "have \[LongDash] words near their inflections, punctuation off in ",
 "its own corner \[LongDash] is not in there yet.  It is useful to ",
 "see the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]before\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] ",
 "picture so we have a baseline to revisit later."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6a7d66d3-5567-416e-84c8-bfe41adddd68"],

