  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " projections for Q, K, V; a ",
 StyleBox["FunctionLayer",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " that computes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox[
   RowBox[{"Q", "\[CenterDot]", 
    SuperscriptBox["K", "\[Transpose]"]}], 
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox["d", "head"]]]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"d3b23a0a-8c6c-44f0-8aff-dc2a1db47e96"],
 " and adds the causal mask; a ",
 StyleBox["SoftmaxLayer",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "; a final ",
 StyleBox["FunctionLayer",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " for the value gather.  Six lines."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b2f13538-c664-4f67-ba3f-9aece351da32"],

Cell["\<\
head = LLMAtoZ`Attention`singleHeadCausalAttention[64, 32, 16];
head\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c5b3f8c3-84ca-48fd-9db1-ddd925ba8a07"],

Cell["Drop the embedder's output into it, get a same-shape output:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"95ea43c3-e27d-466f-8258-aeacf1d007d3"],

Cell["\<\
SeedRandom[42];
x = RandomReal[NormalDistribution[0, 0.1], {16, 64}];
out = head[x];
Dimensions[out]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0964480a-a64d-449c-a60e-347ecce98267"],

Cell["3.4  Multi-head attention", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a132c7a7-8cc1-4fb9-8f7e-1630de1af55c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A single head can only attend in one way at a time.  Multi-head ",
 "attention runs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["n", "heads"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"6aa0bc20-e740-4898-ae5c-94a80b3abbc4"],
 " parallel single-head computations: ",
 "each head applies its own learned projections of the full input ",
 "down to dimension ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "head"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"9df7e460-8ef2-49e2-a386-194451a3c2a7"],
 ", computes attention independently, and produces a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "head"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"9bdfb7f7-6c17-41eb-bcc6-9a6c0c86ee22"],
 "-dimensional output.  The heads are concatenated and a final ",
 "linear projection mixes them back into a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "model"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"dae93639-eaeb-41b2-9784-06d81d57f9cb"],
 "-vector."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9d738884-e8c1-40bb-8e3d-37c65fe689b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The architectural trick is to split ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "model"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"25e6aaba-38ee-4dfa-961d-7ece32d6ad65"],
 " into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["n", "heads"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"32c2f824-8625-41b7-aea7-ff71d1039c87"],
 " equal pieces so the multi-head version has the same parameter ",
 "count as a single-head version at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "model"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"5808693e-7e33-44a3-9a58-d35f191112ed"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8b75c2df-1f0f-4443-bb3a-3ef1005d002a"],

Cell["\<\
mha = LLMAtoZ`Attention`multiHeadAttentionBlock[64, 4, 16];
mha[x] // Dimensions\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"704d0e84-d556-4d4f-bb35-ac33c0e7cbb3"],

Cell["3.5  What real attention looks like: GPT-2 small", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f08da971-e63f-4f34-839c-0645ac0ae7af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We can do something the typical from-scratch tutorial cannot: load ",
 "a fully pretrained language model from ",
 StyleBox["NetModel",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " and look at its actual attention patterns.  GPT-2 small is a ",
 "12-layer transformer with 12 heads per layer at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "model"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"ed48ac78-cf49-4bf4-8517-efcb160145d7"],
 " = 768.  Each block's attention sub-layer holds four learned ",
 "matrices: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["W", "Q"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"9cc221aa-1cbb-4d3f-a0d3-3b6384bcecc6"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["W", "K"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"c23511c9-4d8f-4706-96f2-88ef648f78db"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["W", "V"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"f762211b-f633-4c34-8ae4-0d73c5453be4"],
 " (768\[Times]768 each) plus an output projection.  We have the ",
 "weights; we can recompute the attention weight matrix by hand."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b4d054ca-0cb6-429c-9c70-5655324a3178"],

