Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 5.1.  The signature of the bug, side-by-side.  \
Left: cross-entropy without a softmax wrap descends past zero into \
unbounded-negative territory \[LongDash] not training, just driving one logit \
to +infinity to game an unbounded loss.  Right: with the softmax wrap, proper \
non-negative cross-entropy descends from log(|V|) to a positive asymptote.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"19a21cc5-4c9d-47e4-b1f5-\
a5e5187cfb2d"],

Cell["\<\
This section earns its place because it captures a class of silent error that \
the series has the right tooling to surface, and because it tripped us up \
during development.  The naive way to define the loss is\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"99af90cf-ef33-4df5-9651-37c4ef6b6751"],

Cell["\<\
(* DON'T do this with raw logits *)
(*  NetTrain[..., LossFunction -> CrossEntropyLossLayer[\"Index\"]]  *)\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"eab70ff7-fb9c-4db0-a9b2-d996beb79dbf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["CrossEntropyLossLayer[\"Index\"]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " expects ",
 StyleBox["probabilities",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " as input and computes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", "log"}], 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"p", "[", "target", "]"}], ")"}]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"311ee8d9-0858-42ac-9029-d23c8aa0c7aa"],
 " \[LongDash] non-negative by construction.  Our ",
 StyleBox["gptModel",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " emits raw logits.  Feed logits straight into ",
 StyleBox["CrossEntropyLossLayer[\"Index\"]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " and the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]loss\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] becomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"logit", "[", "target", "]"}], ")"}]}], "+", "constant"}]], 
  "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"6300ce88-9cd3-4036-8624-cdf656a0e025"],
 ", which is unbounded below."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c0befb82-b5ba-4ed1-a393-6ecde0073c7c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For BPE vocab ~4000 this happened to be okay: the optimiser ",
 "couldn't drive a single logit unbounded without similarly moving ",
 "all the others through the shared linear projection, and the ",
 "training landed in regimes that produced sensible token ",
 "distributions.  For a 65-character vocabulary, no such constraint ",
 "applied: the first overnight char-level run, after 6.5 hours, ",
 "produced a model whose maximum logit was ",
 StyleBox["+9,415",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " and whose generations were the single character ",
 StyleBox["'s'",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " repeated to fill the buffer."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c8800c44-4c97-4b60-8596-965d4d2e905b"],

