Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 5.4.  Conceptually: the train/eval gap.  Train \
loss continues to descend; eval loss plateaus.  The growing gap is \
memorisation, not learning.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"65845f2b-1bbf-402b-b0fb-\
3aee9b6b744d"],

Cell["\<\
After 23 rounds, train loss was 0.74.  Held-out eval loss was 2.59, for a \
train/eval ratio of 3.49 \[LongDash] a clear overfit signature.  With 1.8M \
parameters memorising a 1.08M-character corpus, the model has more capacity \
than the data needs and gradient descent preferentially memorises.  Further \
training would push train loss down without making the model actually \
generalise better.  The checkpoint we ship is the one at this point.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"02102b90-dcc1-4cc0-b904-956b1fae1574"],

Cell["6.  Sampling: turning logits into text", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"4d7c1e7d-6e78-4231-8b03-173048341818"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The trained model is a function from a length-",
 Cell[BoxData["L"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"668cc4b8-3e5e-4ccc-b8c4-77d3b7393435"],
 " context window to a length-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"|", "V", "|"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"9bcde62a-6d07-4bcc-b4e7-40b7cad11a7a"],
 " logit vector at every position.  Sampling is the policy that ",
 "turns those logits into a chosen next token.  Five strategies plus ",
 "speculative decoding, all from scratch."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3ec0e1b0-b9ff-44f7-9f5c-81da579d218f"],

Cell["6.1  Temperature", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cc65d3b6-5724-487a-aaf2-91d7fe3ec86c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The simplest dial: softmax-with-temperature.  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
  "p", " ", "\[Proportional]", " ", "exp", "(", "logits", "/", "T", ")"}]], 
  "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"d6318051-b9d5-4673-b3cd-6c16291237a7"],
 ".  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"T", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", "0"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"588729c2-1e20-4ee7-9d39-96f1f1aa6545"],
 " is argmax (greedy); ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"T", " ", "=", " ", "1"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"77e4bd6f-5d3f-4e1a-8ed2-7a6582db0fcd"],
 " is the model's calibrated distribution; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"T", " ", ">", " ", "1"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"4254815d-d374-4b7a-82ea-d65f87218c4f"],
 " softens; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"T", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", "\[Infinity]"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"46f4758b-96b4-43f9-bee2-b1898ca44044"],
 " is uniform.  The same 20-element ",
 "logit vector, five different temperatures \[LongDash] watch how ",
 "the probability mass spreads out:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d51185e2-c52b-48ec-a0ec-423186abc147"],

Cell["\<\
SeedRandom[3]; demoLogits = Sort[
  RandomReal[NormalDistribution[0, 1.5], 20], Greater];
softmaxT[logits_, T_] :=
  LLMAtoZ`Sampling`softmaxTemperature[logits, T];
entropyOf[p_] := -Total[p * Log[p + 1.*^-12]];

GraphicsGrid[
  Partition[
    Table[
      BarChart[softmaxT[demoLogits, T],
        Frame -> True,
        FrameLabel -> {\"token id (sorted by logit)\", \"p\"},
        PlotLabel -> Row[{\"T = \", NumberForm[T, 3],
          \"   entropy = \",
          NumberForm[entropyOf[softmaxT[demoLogits, T]], 3]}],
        PlotRange -> {Automatic, {0, 1}},
        ChartStyle -> ColorData[97][1],
        ImageSize -> 420],
      {T, {0.2, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 3.0}}],
    2, 2, {1, 1}, {}],
  ImageSize -> 900, Spacings -> 8]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"74856930-600e-4225-998e-5bb635068ce0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Figure 6.1.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "  Same logit vector at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"T", " ", "=", " ", "0.2"}], ",", " ", "0.5", ",", " ", "1.0", ",",
    " ", "2.0", ",", " ", "3.0"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"b3c53708-5837-4b5b-88ac-c97ffcde68f8"],
 ".  ",
 "Entropy goes from ~0.6 nats (peaky) to ~3 nats (near-uniform); the ",
 "argmax stays the same, but how often we'd sample it changes ",
 "completely."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1fb24c81-7d9d-4975-9225-e9937f3ffa10"],

Cell["6.1.1  Interactive: the temperature dial", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"ed878fc9-3e86-409a-be6b-99f41fac2c7b"],

Cell["\<\
Drag the slider to retemperature the same distribution and watch the entropy \
update live.  This cell only renders the interactive control when the \
notebook is evaluated in Wolfram Desktop; in the PDF/static view above we \
already showed five fixed snapshots.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c4db062f-7deb-4021-b084-ea5838af5566"],

Cell["\<\
Manipulate[
  BarChart[softmaxT[demoLogits, T],
    Frame -> True, FrameLabel -> {\"token id\", \"probability\"},
    PlotLabel -> Row[{\"T = \", NumberForm[T, 3], \"   entropy = \",
      NumberForm[entropyOf[softmaxT[demoLogits, T]], 3]}],
    PlotRange -> {Automatic, {0, 1}},
    ChartStyle -> ColorData[97][1], ImageSize -> 700],
  {{T, 1.0, \"temperature\"}, 0.05, 3.0, 0.05, Appearance -> \"Labeled\"},
  ControlPlacement -> Top]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3f19cfa7-151b-4521-8752-e7b0cea581d5"],

Cell["6.2  Top-k and top-p (nucleus)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"de807359-8ab5-451e-8f2b-8d54f8cdeb0e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Truncation strategies.  ",
 StyleBox["Top-k",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " keeps the ",
 Cell[BoxData["k"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"2d5835c3-a752-488d-9238-7f79a9178176"],
 " highest-probability tokens before re-normalising.  ",
 StyleBox["Top-p",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (nucleus, Holtzman et al. 2020) keeps the smallest set whose ",
 "cumulative probability exceeds ",
 Cell[BoxData["p"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"43204411-821e-44f4-b93b-c6131dc34379"],
 ".  Top-p adapts the cutoff to the local sharpness of the ",
 "distribution."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"19f1fda4-1843-47ad-ad99-41e63ada9489"],

Cell["\<\
SeedRandom[7]; demoP =
  N @ Normalize[Sort[Exp[RandomReal[NormalDistribution[0, 1.2], 20]],
                      Greater], Total];

drawTopK[k_] := BarChart[
  ReplacePart[demoP,
    Thread[Range[k + 1, Length[demoP]] -> 0.]],
  Frame -> True,
  FrameLabel -> {\"token id (rank order)\", \"p\"},
  PlotLabel -> Row[{\"top-k, k = \", k}],
  PlotRange -> {Automatic, {0, Max[demoP] * 1.05}},
  ChartStyle -> ColorData[97][1], ImageSize -> 420];

drawTopP[p_] := Module[
  {sorted = demoP, cum, cut, kept},
  cum = Accumulate[sorted];
  cut = LengthWhile[cum, # <= p &] + 1;
  kept = ReplacePart[sorted,
    Thread[Range[cut + 1, Length[sorted]] -> 0.]];
  BarChart[kept, Frame -> True,
    FrameLabel -> {\"token id (rank order)\", \"p\"},
    PlotLabel -> Row[{\"top-p, p = \", p,
      \"   (kept \", cut, \" tokens)\"}],
    PlotRange -> {Automatic, {0, Max[demoP] * 1.05}},
    ChartStyle -> ColorData[97][2], ImageSize -> 420]];

GraphicsGrid[{
  {drawTopK[3], drawTopP[0.5]},
  {drawTopK[5], drawTopP[0.8]},
  {drawTopK[10], drawTopP[0.95]}},
  ImageSize -> 900, Spacings -> 8]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0451697d-1264-4b99-9feb-69bf76a5336f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Figure 6.2.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "  Same 20-token probability row, three top-k cutoffs vs three ",
 "top-p cutoffs.  Notice that top-p with ",
 Cell[BoxData["p"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"a36451f2-91b8-467f-9456-3a3318898a42"],
 " = 0.95 ",
 "automatically expands the kept set when the head is flat and ",
 "contracts it when the head is sharp \[LongDash] something a fixed ",
 Cell[BoxData["k"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"56a01b5e-c9d5-4788-9f08-44035cf2855d"],
 " can't do."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a77b00aa-d5c4-4cfe-8aae-c3be0470bdb9"],

Cell["6.3  Beam search", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c71640e7-2a5a-4a35-908d-978b3371d856"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For translation-style tasks where one answer is correct, beam ",
 "search is the deterministic alternative.  Track ",
 StyleBox["beamWidth",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " most likely partial sequences at every step; at the end return ",
 "the highest-scoring complete one.  Rare in generative LLMs but ",
 "still common in machine translation."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3078f0bb-d297-4bbe-9692-d839a9533c11"],

Cell["6.4  Speculative decoding", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9a94f138-1949-40c8-9c46-dfbca785f385"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A small draft model proposes ",
 Cell[BoxData["k"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"d4815bb5-881a-433f-98dc-653f7114e47c"],
 " tokens autoregressively; the main model verifies them in a single ",
 "forward pass; accepted tokens commit, the first rejected token is ",
 "resampled.  Useful when the draft is much cheaper than the main."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2df63644-d6c5-4e40-ab14-ddd93ad3e24b"],

