Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 7.2.  LoRA decomposition.  The frozen \
pretrained weight W is left alone; two small matrices A (8x768) and B (768x8) \
are added.  Effective weight: W + B.A.  Trainable parameters: 12K vs 589K, a \
48-fold reduction.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"78e440b1-2fa6-4d1a-b1cc-\
a43bbc33cbc5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Full SFT updates every weight in the pretrained model.  ",
 StyleBox["LoRA",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (Hu et al. 2021) updates a tiny fraction.  For each linear ",
 "layer with weight ",
 Cell[BoxData["W"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"c80ed584-f78e-482a-b7ea-0b141505fed7"],
 " of shape ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["d", "in"], "\[Times]", 
   SubscriptBox["d", "out"]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"3df3b33a-cb99-4c92-8417-3247b7e56e5b"],
 ", freeze ",
 Cell[BoxData["W"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"46b87961-3dab-4b8a-bd0d-2e887759137d"],
 " and learn two small matrices ",
 Cell[BoxData["A"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"7c9d44df-61a3-416e-8974-e9593d16d2ec"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["B"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"dcffe352-be19-4d92-aeb2-b672b242e4ab"],
 " of rank ",
 Cell[BoxData["r"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"f73a2b8c-20a0-4173-80b9-2043cfabb207"],
 " so the effective weight at inference is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"W", "+", "BA"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"5cd59799-7c90-4b38-938f-cb2adfd2c1f3"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"27ac1f3e-a5e8-4b46-81ef-87ee577a647c"],

Cell["\<\
LLMAtoZ`Lora`loraParameterCount[768, 768, #] & /@ {4, 8, 16, 32, 64}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8fbc6294-db6e-4ac6-9d43-bf44a7d79f8d"],

Cell["\<\
12K LoRA parameters per 768\[Times]768 layer at rank 8 versus 590K for full \
fine-tuning.  48\[Times] reduction per layer; with 12 layers and four \
LoRA-wrapped projections per block (Q, K, V, O), the total trainable \
parameter count drops to ~1.2M vs 28M for full SFT.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1ae39984-c6df-48f7-b7ac-90ce8ef1207d"],

Cell["7.4  Classification fine-tuning (Raschka chapter 6)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1820d6f1-93e7-40f3-af26-284c578a0b62"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Same pretrained model, different task.  Strip the LM head, pool ",
 "the last-position hidden state with a ",
 StyleBox["SequenceLastLayer",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", project to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["n", "classes"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"5f8cc2be-0af6-44d5-b2e0-6f1842b7193f"],
 " logits.  ",
 "The rest of the pretrained backbone is reused as-is."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"edd42ee3-4310-4b37-b1b1-ac34e5bb6b77"],

Cell["\<\
(* Demo: classify Shakespeare excerpts as tragedy vs comedy *)
LLMAtoZ`Classification`shakespeareGenreLabels[][[1 ;; 4]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b6c8d949-ff1a-43b4-bf49-21dd34c0f8f8"],

Cell["8.  Reinforcement learning post-training", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"6e2fc13d-ac64-4fe3-bd68-c6161d7c5f16"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "SFT teaches the model to imitate.  RL teaches it to optimise.  ",
 "After SFT, we take the model, sample completions on a task with a ",
 "verifiable reward (or a reward model), and update the policy to ",
 "make high-reward completions more likely.  Following nanochat we ",
 "use ",
 StyleBox["GRPO",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " in its simplest form: no reference model, no KL term, just ",
 "centred advantages over a group of rollouts."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7f494a6d-5ec0-4c05-b302-949e0f6bf133"],

