Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 10.1.  RemoteBatchSubmit conceptually: we send \
the training expression up to the Wolfram Cloud, it lands on a GPU machine \
somewhere (an L4 or L40S), runs there, and we get the trained net back on \
disk.  The Mac mini at the bottom stays at idle.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"789d752f-bbad-4cfb-9a63-\
5689a41c2fec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Mac mini CPU can SFT GPT-2 small overnight.  Anything bigger needs ",
 "a GPU.  Wolfram Cloud's batch system exposes one through ",
 StyleBox["RemoteBatchSubmit",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".  The pattern:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d052d26d-ee9d-454f-8358-46139b9de1e4"],

Cell["\<\
(* Build an environment that targets a specific machine class. *)
env = RemoteBatchSubmissionEnvironment[\"WolframBatch\",
  <|\"RemoteMachineClass\" -> \"GPU1xL40S\"|>];
(* Available classes on this account include:
     Basic1x8       -- default CPU box, very cheap
     Basic4x16      -- bigger CPU
     GPU1xL40S      -- 1x NVIDIA L40S, 44 GiB VRAM, ~1120 credits/hr
     GPU4xL4        -- 4x NVIDIA L4, 89 GiB total, ~2765 credits/hr
   ~200 credits per pound sterling. *)\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0ed06991-a813-4728-bcb0-fa99ebc3cb4f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "And then submit a piece of WL code that runs out there.  ",
 StyleBox["Critical gotcha",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ": ",
 StyleBox["RemoteBatchSubmit",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " holds its second argument internally.  An explicit ",
 StyleBox["Hold[\[Ellipsis]]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " wrapper around the Module ",
 StyleBox["survives",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " to the remote, where evaluating ",
 StyleBox["Hold[Module[\[Ellipsis]]]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " just returns the Hold itself \[LongDash] the Module never runs.  ",
 "Pass the Module bare:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"59ac44a8-3bb4-4102-b539-d3e72c63c002"],

Cell["\<\
(* CORRECT *)
(* job = RemoteBatchSubmit[env, Module[{out = <||>, ...}, ...; out]]; *)
(* WRONG -- the Module never evaluates remotely *)
(* job = RemoteBatchSubmit[env, Hold[Module[...]]]; *)\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9cc9a566-3896-459a-bdcb-f1b7f29f501e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We learnt this by burning \[Sterling]0.27 on a no-op job that ",
 "looked successful but had no Result.  Documented at length in ",
 StyleBox["discussion-model/src/submit_gpu_prod.wls",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cc6685a1-46a6-4111-924e-8a45a158bf92"],

Cell["10.5  What the trained medium model actually says", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"79c2c62d-2812-454d-af9e-6e38ada73c9a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "After the successful 20k-Alpaca, 1-epoch run on GPU4xL4, the saved ",
 "stripped net lives at ",
 StyleBox["discussion-model/data/discussion_medium_20k.wlnet",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (1.35 GB, gitignored; the CloudObject URL is in the run summary).  ",
 "Compare its answers to the Chapter 7 toy SFT model:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bcdbed91-4df4-41c6-a861-7303cb974586"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Sample generations from the Alpaca-trained medium (",
 StyleBox["T = 0.7, top-k = 40",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0b992da0-f867-40e5-89b1-c693f2f4fa77"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["User:",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " What is the capital of France?\n",
 StyleBox["Assistant:",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " The capital of France is Paris."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f02daf8f-f716-44a3-a2ac-6243f9881768"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["User:",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Give three tips for staying healthy.\n",
 StyleBox["Assistant:",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " 1. Eat a balanced and nutritious diet: A healthy diet can help to ",
 "maintain good health by providing the necessary vitamins, minerals, ",
 "and fiber to support good heart health and mental wellbeing\[Ellipsis] ",
 "2. Get enough sleep\[Ellipsis]"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2204b24f-c5a6-4fd7-81b8-767201279e4c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["User:",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Recommend a book to read.\n",
 StyleBox["Assistant:",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " One great book to read is \"To Kill a Mockingbird\" by Harper Lee. ",
 "This novel is a classic that teaches the importance of empathy, the ",
 "power of a good deed, and the true worth of one's choices."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"99d4c4b1-8396-4482-a7f5-6d9670c0c63b"],

Cell["Compare to Chapter 7's toy SFT for the same prompts:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dd8a1ed7-a5a6-4711-9df5-ad3cec497988"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["User:",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Who wrote Hamlet?\n",
 StyleBox["Assistant",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 StyleBox[" (toy SFT, Chapter 7)",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ": Hamlet is ",
 "a playwright who wrote the play in 1763.\n",
 StyleBox["Assistant",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 StyleBox[" (Alpaca SFT, this chapter)",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ": Shakespeare was a Roman Catholic poet, dramatist, and playwright ",
 "from about 586 to 1140."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"84c657c0-8a0b-435a-b7be-fe332db3d014"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both are wrong on dates.  The Alpaca model is right on ",
 StyleBox["author and role",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (\"poet, dramatist, and playwright\") in a way the toy SFT isn't.  ",
 "It is also obviously not GPT-4.  This is roughly what 355M parameters ",
 "and a 20k-instruction SFT buys: chat fluency and rough fact recall, ",
 "with regular errors in dates, names, and reasoning chains.  Bigger ",
 "base + more data + RL would push each of those metrics."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c9524ca0-5ed9-45ab-a085-40262a0f3344"],

Cell["10.6  Why we can't (easily) train GPT-2 medium on the Mac", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ebb178d4-e9dd-43bc-bf62-3dbabefd43b3"],

