Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 10.2.  Out-of-memory: trying to save a 3 GB \
GPT-2 large checkpoint on a 24 GiB single-GPU L4 after training fills the \
device.  Training itself succeeded; the post-training NetTake + CloudPut \
cascade did not.  Twice.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"91b8d3ed-28a2-46cf-8ba4-\
905b0c2eee3f"],

Cell["\<\
The same surgery code that works on GPT-2 small (124M) hits a specific \
low-level bug on GPT-2 medium when run on Mac CPU.  The error is at the MXNet \
operator level:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5cc8ae08-c40a-44ae-aef8-c418808339c1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["MXNetError: Check failed: assign(&dattr, vec.at(i)): \n",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 StyleBox["Incompatible attr in node _copyto at 0-th output: \n",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 StyleBox["expected [4096], got [1024]\n",
  FontFamily->"Courier"]
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8987148a-5465-4cde-be18-eb09b2cbfddd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The numbers 1024 and 4096 are GPT-2 medium's ",
 StyleBox["d_model",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["d_ff",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".  Something in the gradient routing across our reconstructed chain ",
 "gets confused at this exact size.  Same code, same call, works ",
 "perfectly on cuDNN (cloud GPU) and on MXNet-CPU at small.  Not ",
 "fixable from the application layer.  Practical implication: ",
 "anything bigger than small needs the cloud."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cbb8c395-6647-442e-a014-c580217cb8bb"],

Cell["10.7  Inference is slow in Wolfram Language on Mac", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a9a42348-3f4c-4fc5-8e85-9790857f50ce"],

